{"id":"180efadb94f279cb","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-anfuniq.md","title":"Existence and uniqueness of algebraic normal form","display":"thm-anfuniq — Existence and uniqueness of algebraic normal form","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-anfuniq","aliases":["27-thm-anfuniq"],"display":"thm-anfuniq — Existence and uniqueness of algebraic normal form","depends_on":["[[27-df-anf]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§1.12.1 Theorem 1.33 and proof","source_printed_pages":"44–45","source_pdf_pages":"68–69","verification_status":"source-statement-and-proof-checked-alternative-inversion-proof"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-anfuniq"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-anfuniq</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-anfuniq — Existence and uniqueness of algebraic normal form"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"94b5a40ac9e27f34\" href=\"?note=94b5a40ac9e27f34\" title=\"27-df-anf\">27-df-anf</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§1.12.1 Theorem 1.33 and proof"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"44–45"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"68–69"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-and-proof-checked-alternative-inversion-proof"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\">\\(f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha_f\">\\(\\alpha_f\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ANF}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{ANF}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"94b5a40ac9e27f34\" href=\"?note=94b5a40ac9e27f34\" title=\"27-df-anf\">27-df-anf</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ANF}_n(\\alpha_f)=f,\\qquad\\forall c\\in\\mathbb B^{\\mathcal P([n])}\\;(\\mathrm{ANF}_n(c)=f\\Rightarrow c=\\alpha_f).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ANF}_n(\\alpha_f)=f,\\qquad\\forall c\\in\\mathbb B^{\\mathcal P([n])}\\;(\\mathrm{ANF}_n(c)=f\\Rightarrow c=\\alpha_f).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>在点 χ_A 上只留下 S⊆A 的单项式。对子集再次异或反演时，一个真子集的出现次数为 2 的正幂，模 2 消去；只有 A 本身留一次。这既给存在也给唯一性，与书中结构归纳加计数的证明互相对应。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-anf","status":"resolved","id":"94b5a40ac9e27f34","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-anf]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-anf","status":"resolved","id":"94b5a40ac9e27f34","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n$；$\\alpha_f$、$\\mathrm{ANF}_n$ 见 [[27-df-anf]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\alpha_f","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ANF}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ANF}_n(\\alpha_f)=f,\\qquad\\forall c\\in\\mathbb B^{\\mathcal P([n])}\\;(\\mathrm{ANF}_n(c)=f\\Rightarrow c=\\alpha_f).","display":true}],"bytes":1267,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-369","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-anfuniq|thm-anfuniq — Existence and uniqueness of algebraic normal form]]"}],"outgoing":["94b5a40ac9e27f34"]}